One suggestion, 
according to what you say above, if you sharpen a +0 longsword with a 
+3 whetstone, the longsword becomes +1, and the whetstone +2, sharpen it
again and you're left with a +2 longsword and a +1 whetstone.  So since
you can't sharpen a +2 longsword with a +1 whetstone, you CAN'T get the
+0 longsword to +3 with only a +3 whetstone...
 
So maybe you SHOULD be able to use a whetstone for a couple of times
before it loses a bonus...
 
